{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814227-ideas-for-developing-a-feeding-focused-game-style","id":814227,"title":"Ideas for developing a feeding focused game style?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-22T10:20:46-08:00","id":814227,"title":"Ideas for developing a feeding focused game style?","content":"Reading through the V:tR 2e book, I ran into the idea of twists on the standard mechanical system designed to promote a certain aspect of the game. One thing I immediately took notice of was the section called &quot;Above All, Feed&quot; (2e core, p. 276). It suggests a highly simplified system where you simply let your Vitae equal your dice pools, and you may spend them on actions as you wish. This naturally makes feeding become the overarching concern, since you'd chug much more fuel this way (I think?).<br /> <br /> This idea appealed to me since 1) I have no earlier experience with the game and I'd like to try it out in a way that's not too much hassle, and in a way that lets me attempt it in a chat environment without a scene literally taking three hours, and 2) the theme of feeding and power/addiction contrast is one of the things that made me interested in checking out Vampire more.<br /> <br /> So while I'm very interested in the idea, the book does say that twists are only conceptual ideas, and I'll need to refine it myself for my own needs. Given my lack of experience, I thought I'd turn to you here.<br /> <br /> My thoughts so far are these: Simplicity is king. I don't think I want a lot of interdependent parts, providing passive bonuses and such, because the form of just looking at your Vitae pool and deciding how many dice you want is so clean. I could simply say Vitae and Health are the only stats in the game. My formulation of the system so far goes like this, though:<br /> <br /> \u00a4 You can take any action you like. You will always roll a chance die unless you add dice by spending Vitae at a 1-for-1 rate. The only other type of bonuses and penalties are circumstantial.<br /> \u00a4 Kindred can hold 15 Vitae. They may spend any amount of Vitae at once.<br /> \u00a4 Other things that cost Vitae: Waking up from daysleep, and any action where the Kindred specifically use their blood (ghouling, sacrifice).<br /> <br /> \u00a4 Kindred may Frenzy as normal. Frenzy can be resisted by rolling (current Vitae)/2. The hungrier the Beast is, the more likely it is to emerge. A Kindred in Frenzy can't control their actions, but only seek to remove the source of the provocation as quickly as possible.<br /> <br /> \u00a4 Kindred can lose and gain Humanity as normal. Detachment rolls are always a chance die. On a dramatic failure, the Kindred descends a step on the Humanity scale. There should probably be a way of gaining Humanity too, but let's be real, it's losing that's going to be important.<br /> <br /> \u00a4 Blood bonds should also be a thing.<br /> <br /> Ideas? Comments? Condemnations? :3<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T10:34:15-08:00","id":814239,"title":"","content":"Or you could make vampires having to spend an amount equal to their blood potency in order to wake up each night. That would certainly add a degree of urgency to feeding each night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T12:18:36-08:00","id":814361,"title":"","content":"The Above All, Feed system is too barebones for my taste. If I wanted to run a feeding heavy game, I'd just have everyone play Revenants. But, if you want a super simple system like this one, more power to you. I'd say keep it as close to the Above All, Feed rules as you can. Barebones systems don't tend to support subsystems very well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T12:29:35-08:00","id":814380,"title":"","content":"You might be interested in <a href=\"https://enigmamachinations.files.wordpress.com/2015/06/undying.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Undying</a>.<br /> <br /> It's pretty much a diceless version of VtR.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link